cudakmeans
==========

The same k means as in ../kmeans, with the assignment step moved to the
graphics card.

Every point has to be measured against every centroid and none of those
measurements depend on each other, so it is one thread per point. The
centroids are the same for the whole block and go into shared memory once
per block instead of being read from global memory k times per point.

The update step stays on the host: it is a few sums over k clusters, and
doing it on the card means atomics or a reduction pass for no real gain.

    make && ./cudakmeans_test

Without a card the host tests still run and the gpu ones are skipped.
There is also make emu, which builds the kernel for the cpu.
